# 05. Archive and Edition Navigation

WORLD SIGNAL publishes one cumulative edition per local calendar date.

There are three editorial updates:

- Morning.
- Midday.
- Evening.

These are revisions of the same daily edition.

The frontend must not display them as three separate editions.

### Archive requirements

Build a polished archive navigation experience.

Readers should be able to:

- Open the latest available edition.
- Browse earlier dates.
- Select an edition by date.
- See its last updated time.
- See its publication status.
- Move between previous and next available editions.

Do not assume every calendar date has an edition.

Use the actual archive index.

The archive must remain functional as the number of daily editions grows.

