# 07. Security and Content Integrity

Markdown and YAML must be treated as untrusted input.

Required safeguards:

- Never execute Markdown code fences.
- Never inject arbitrary HTML.
- Never use unsafe HTML rendering.
- Sanitize rendered Markdown.
- Only allow HTTP and HTTPS external links.
- Preserve canonical source URLs.
- Validate index paths before fetching.
- Prevent external URLs or path traversal from being treated as edition resources.
- Handle malformed YAML safely.
- Never execute scripts from editorial content.

Editorial content must remain read-only within the frontend.

Do not modify claims, source records, or analytical statements while rendering them.

